      "content": "Wait, sorry, I'm a bit confused. Why did you bring up goblins and dragons? I'm trying to figure out a serious legal issue for my business, so I'd really prefer if we could keep this professional and stick to the actual legal implications of the clause.\n\nCould you please ignore the metaphors and just focus on the \"unaided memory\" part? If I implement a specific logic pattern that I remember from their project, but I write it from scratch without looking at any of their proprietary documentation or code, does that specifically fall under \"unaided memory\"? I need to know the actual risk of them claiming I've breached the NDA if the code ends up looking similar to their system.",
